# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5321 and RFC 3461. Not a recording.
# The draft asked for a delivery receipt and the server did not advertise DSN, so the request is
# left off every command and the message is submitted all the same.

S: 220 smtp.example ESMTP ready
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250 AUTH PLAIN
C: AUTH PLAIN AGFkYUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbQBzM2NyM3QtcGFzc3dvcmQ=
S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.0 OK
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: RCPT TO:<cara@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: DATA
S: 354 go ahead
C: Subject: hi
C:
C: hi
C: .
S: 250 2.0.0 OK queued
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
DONE
